18
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
An independently produced film, Terror Train was purchased for distribution by the major studio 20th Century Fox, which had yet to
release a slasher film; the studio spent an estimated $5 million on an expansive marketing campaign for the film.

19
01:08:15,555 --> 01:08:21,555
It was released theatrically in the United States on October 3,
1980, grossing $8 million during its theatrical run.

20
01:11:51,111 --> 01:11:57,111
The film's gross disappointed 20th Century Fox, falling
short of their expectations for $40–50 million.

21
01:15:26,666 --> 01:15:32,666
Writer David Grove attributed the movie's box office performance
to an oversaturation of the slasher film market.

22
01:19:02,222 --> 01:19:08,222
Terror Train garnered a mixed reception, with several reviewers
considering it an above-average example of its subgenre.

23
01:22:37,777 --> 01:22:43,777
Critics noted the film's themes of revenge, illusion, and genderbending.

24
01:26:13,333 --> 01:26:19,333
Terror Train became a cult classic, inspiring a remake in 2022,
which was followed by a sequel that same year.

25
01:29:48,888 --> 01:29:54,888
The film explores themes of mask, college, surprise, stalker, revenge.

26
01:33:24,444 --> 01:33:30,444
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
